{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"text":" slice, fetches a Swidux-defined JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a — same input always produces the same bucket, no network round-trip per read. Local overrides give QA a one-action toggle that wins over remote evaluation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an API-level reference, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference"},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes you have a Swidux app already wired up — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You also need somewhere to host a JSON file. Any URL works — Cloudflare Pages, R2, S3, a Worker, your own backend. The plugin doesn’t care. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/"},{"type":"text","text":" is a runnable Cloudflare Worker that serves feature-flag "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"text":" killswitch config for every app in a portfolio from one URL and one KV namespace, keyed ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/<appID>\/<resource>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — point this plugin at ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxFeatureFlags\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 2: Add a state slice and action case","anchor":"Step-2-Add-a-state-slice-and-action-case","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxFeatureFlags","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var featureFlags: FeatureFlagsState = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case featureFlags(FeatureFlagsAction)","    \/\/ ... your other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" is needed in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file that touches "},{"code":"store.featureFlags.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — including views that read flags for display. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"tip"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Hydrate state and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-3-Hydrate-state-and-register-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At app launch, hydrate state from your ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (so the install ID and last-known-good config survive cold launches), then register the plugin:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv)",")","","let store = Store(initialState: initial, reducer: AppReducer())","","\/\/ With the Examples\/ConfigWorker setup this is the shared portfolio URL:","\/\/ \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\". Any URL returning FeatureFlagsConfig works.","let configURL = URL(static: \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\")","","let flags = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags,","    action: AppAction.featureFlags,","    extractAction: { if case .featureFlags(let a) = $0 { return a } else { return nil } },","    service: HTTPFeatureFlagsService(url: configURL),","    keyValueStore: kv",")","store.register(plugin: flags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 4: Declare typed flag keys","anchor":"Step-4-Declare-typed-flag-keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each flag once on a namespace so reads are type-safe:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension BoolFlag {","    static let newOnboarding = BoolFlag(\"new_onboarding\")","}","","enum CheckoutVariant: String { case control, treatment }","","extension VariantFlag where Variant == CheckoutVariant {","    static let checkoutLayout = VariantFlag(\"checkout_layout\", default: .control)","}","","extension ValueFlag where Value == Int {","    static let maxFreeUploads = ValueFlag(\"max_free_uploads\", default: 5)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 5: Read flags from views","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-5-Read-flags-from-views"},{"code":["if store.featureFlags.isEnabled(.newOnboarding) {","    NewOnboardingView()","}","","let layout = store.featureFlags.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","let cap = store.featureFlags.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 6: Refresh on foreground","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-6-Refresh-on-foreground"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin debounces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"text":" against the configured ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RefreshPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":", so it’s safe to dispatch on every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scenePhase"},{"text":" transition:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .active { store.send(.featureFlags(.refresh)) }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For wire format, bucketing, and exposure tracking details, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Add Feature Flags","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with 